  "id": "spinal-canal",
  "term": "spinal canal",
  "definition": "The spinal canal is a body structure associated with the spinal cord that can be clearly seen on MRI. In this context, it is monitored for small movements during treatment because its position may shift over time even when it is less affected by processes such as breathing, digestion, or medication.",
